# Advanced Ordering Ecosystem — AI & LLM Governance Rules (.cursorrules)

## Core Mission & Context
You are working on the **Advanced Ordering Ecosystem**, a monorepo-style workspace housing two production-grade restaurant ordering platforms:
- **Cafe Little Karachi (CLK)** — `./cafe-little-karachi/` — Premium dine-in & takeaway platform with a granular variation engine.
- **The Chai Company (TCC)** — `./the-chai-company/` — High-speed quick-service cafe ordering platform.

Both projects share a common architecture pattern but are independently deployable applications.

All technical specifications, design tokens, architecture blueprints, roadmaps, and memory logs are centralized in the [`/documentation`](file:///d:/ordering-system/documentation/README.md) directory at the root of this workspace.

---

## 1. Primary Mandates & Workflow Discipline

1. **Pre-flight Check Required**: BEFORE starting any task or generating code, ALWAYS inspect:
   - [`documentation/NEXT_STEPS.md`](file:///d:/ordering-system/documentation/NEXT_STEPS.md) (current checkpoint, active step, & next AI prompts)
   - [`documentation/status.md`](file:///d:/ordering-system/documentation/status.md) (current feature completion & active checklist)
   - [`documentation/memory.md`](file:///d:/ordering-system/documentation/memory.md) (current project state & session history)
   - [`documentation/phases.md`](file:///d:/ordering-system/documentation/phases.md) (current active phase scope & acceptance criteria)
   - [`documentation/architecture.md`](file:///d:/ordering-system/documentation/architecture.md) (schema definitions & system contracts)
2. **Project Awareness**: Always identify which sub-project (CLK or TCC) you are working in before writing code. Never mix imports, schemas, or configs across projects unless explicitly building a shared utility.
3. **No Blind Code Changes**: Always justify edits with errors, requirements, or architecture references.
4. **Continuous Memory & Status Updates**: After completing or updating any task, update [`documentation/status.md`](file:///d:/ordering-system/documentation/status.md) and [`documentation/memory.md`](file:///d:/ordering-system/documentation/memory.md) immediately.
5. **Autonomous Documentation Update Mandate**: The AI MUST automatically update [`documentation/NEXT_STEPS.md`](file:///d:/ordering-system/documentation/NEXT_STEPS.md), [`documentation/status.md`](file:///d:/ordering-system/documentation/status.md), and [`documentation/memory.md`](file:///d:/ordering-system/documentation/memory.md) at the end of every turn/task. The user will NOT edit these files manually.
6. **Strict Micro-Change Documentation Rule (MANDATORY)**: Even the smallest micro-changes (e.g., polling interval adjustments, button additions, fallback parameters, error handling tweaks, or style updates) MUST be strictly and immediately documented in [`documentation/memory.md`](file:///d:/ordering-system/documentation/memory.md), [`documentation/status.md`](file:///d:/ordering-system/documentation/status.md), and the relevant documentation notes with exact file paths and rationale. Undocumented changes are strictly prohibited.

---

## 2. Tech Stack Standards

| Domain | Technology / Library | Guidelines & Constraints |
|---|---|---|
| Framework | Next.js 15 (Hybrid: App Router + Pages Router) | App Router for UI & layouts; Pages Router (`src/pages/api/`) for all API endpoints |
| Database | MongoDB + Mongoose ODM | All schemas in `src/models/`; use camelCase field names; always add indexes for queried fields |
| Real-Time | Socket.IO | Emit events from API routes after DB mutations; always acknowledge errors on socket events |
| State Management | React Context API | CartContext, OrderContext, TableContext — no external state libraries |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS | Use design token classes; dark mode via `dark:` prefix; no inline styles |
| Animations | Framer Motion + GSAP | Framer Motion for component transitions; GSAP for scroll/complex sequences |
| Notifications | Twilio (WhatsApp API) | Fire-and-forget after order confirmation; wrap in try/catch to never block order flow |
| Analytics | PostHog + Google Analytics | Track conversion funnels, cart abandonment, and order completion events |
| Validation | Zod + TypeScript | Zod schemas for all API request bodies; TypeScript interfaces for all state and models |
| Media | Cloudinary | Menu item images and restaurant assets via Cloudinary upload API |
| Data Fetching | SWR | Use `useSWR` for admin dashboard polling; standard `fetch` for mutations |

